{
  "version": "2025.10",
  "description": "Typography — responsive type scale.\n\nEvery size and line height is multiplied by --typography-scale (1 when unset;\nset by [data-a63-type-scale] and the .text-scale-* classes). The Viewport\nmodifier holds the three steps: xs (the base values), sm (640px+ / tablet\nportrait) and md (768px+ / tablet landscape and up). Each step is written twice,\nfrom the same values: as a min-width @media breakpoint on :root that declares\nonly what changes from the step before, and as a complete [data-window-size]\nrule (md also covers lg and xl) for windowed layouts. The window rules come\nlast, so on an element that matches both, the window size wins.",
  "sets": {
